{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"Under [Rule 12d1-4](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/270.12d1-4):\n\n- **Acquiring fund’s adviser:** Evaluate the investment structure’s complexity and relevant fees and expenses, and find that the acquiring fund’s fees and expenses do not duplicate the acquired fund’s.\n- **Acquired fund’s adviser:** Find that undue-influence concerns are reasonably addressed, considering investment size/limits, anticipated redemption timing, advance-notice arrangements, and potential in-kind redemptions.\n- **Interfund agreement:** Unless both funds have the same investment adviser, execute a fund-of-funds investment agreement before exceeding statutory limits. It must include material terms supporting the required findings, permit either fund to terminate on no more than 60 days’ written notice, and require reasonably requested acquired-fund fee/expense information.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Advisers must make findings before exceeding statutory limits, revisit them periodically as appropriate, and report their evaluations, findings, and supporting bases to their respective boards by the next regularly scheduled meeting."}}
